1
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:10,117
I want to see what
virtual reality is like.

2
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,720
I wonder when I first thought that.

3
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:20,420
I used to hate virtual reality
games with a vengeance,

4
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,115
and I blamed them for stealing
my brother away from me.

5
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:29,017
but later on i got
curious i didn't know why

6
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,629
my brother loved them
so much so i figured.

7
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,080
maybe i should see why for myself.

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,497
i didn't know what to
expect at first but after a

9
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,077
while i was surprised by
how much i loved alfheim.

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:51,397
online it was amazing
flying through the sky

11
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:55,077
on my very own wings to
fly as far as i wanted.

12
00:00:55,160 --> 00:01:01,100
as high as i wanted as fast as i wanted
i'd give anything and everything for that.

13
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:08,360
i think i get it now i can see why
my brother loves the virtual world.

14
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:49,040
If I'm here, I won't be
able to see the future.

15
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:55,860
I won't be able to see the sun again.

16
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:00,157
I'm going to cry.

17
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,720
If this is my dream, F

18
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,200
Hold it, Lefa! Huh!?

19
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:59,980
I thought I told you not to call me
that at school, Nagata. Didn't I?

20
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,180
Yeah, you did.

21
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,680
Sorry, Suguha. Idiot!

22
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,700
I'm sorry, I meant Kirigaya!

23
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:08,340
What do you want?

24
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:10,137
Wait, why are you even here?

25
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:13,177
You got a release from taking
the high school entrance exams.

26
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:15,737
They're not making you
come anyway, are they?

27
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:16,650
Sugu!

28
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,950
Kirigaya!

29
00:03:18,033 --> 00:03:20,954
I need to talk to you, so
I've been waiting all morning.

30
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,597
Wait, you're not here
for the exams, are you?

31
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,510
No.

32
00:03:24,593 --> 00:03:28,066
The advisor for the kendo club
asked me to come in, that's all.

33
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:29,260
Well, what's up?

34
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:31,317
It's Sigurd and the others.

35
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,217
They all wanted to go
hunting again this afternoon.

36
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:35,130
Sorry.

37
00:03:35,213 --> 00:03:37,377
I won't be going out with
those guys for a while.

38
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,420
Wait, what? Why not?

39
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,317
I've got plans to head
over to Arun, that's why.

40
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:45,047
But isn't Arun at the
base of the world tree?

41
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,517
Wait a second! You... are you...

42
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,157
you're not going with that spriggan!

43
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,070
Yeah.

44
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,240
Well, sort of.

45
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,537
I promised I'd show him how to get there.

46
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:57,561
But have you thought about
what you're doing, Lee?

47
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,837
Kitty Gaia, it's just so far away,

48
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,957
and you guys will be sleeping
together, and they'll...

49
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,687
Don't get any weird
ideas about it, you jerk!

50
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:13,697
Look, I've made up my
mind, and that's that.

51
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:16,133
Say hey to Sigurd and the others for me.

52
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,550
See you later.

53
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,716
All I'm doing is showing him the way.

54
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,675
That's all I'm doing.

55
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:54,740
Link, start!

56
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,840
Hey there, been waiting long?

57
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:16,880
Not at all, I just walked in.

58
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:19,495
Actually, I was out shopping for gear.

59
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,357
Oh, that's right.

60
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:23,137
I should update my equipment, too.

61
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:25,632
I don't think this is going to be enough.

62
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,030
Okay.

63
00:05:27,113 --> 00:05:29,020
I know a good weapon shop in town.

64
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,497
But do you have enough money?

65
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,109
Because they're not cheap.

66
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:34,410
Okay, money.

67
00:05:34,493 --> 00:05:36,997
Wait, this thing called
Yule, is that money?

68
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:37,910
Uh-huh.

69
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:43,160
Hey, Yui, wake up. We're heading out now.

70
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:45,410
Okay.

71
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:10,698
Why'd we come here?

72
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:15,804
Well, when flying long distances, it's
better if you start from a higher altitude.

73
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,877
That's what the tower's here for.

74
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,600
Oh, that makes sense.

75
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,120
You're kidding me!

76
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,120
Come on, let's go!

77
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,811
I want to get past the forest before dark.

78
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,020
This way, Slowpoke!

79
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:42,670
Leafa!

80
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,120
Oh, uh, hello, Sigurd.

81
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,577
What's this I hear about
you leaving the party?

82
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:50,490
Is that true?

83
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,600
Well, yeah, it is.

84
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:56,897
Do you have any idea how much that's
going to upset the other members?

85
00:06:56,980 --> 00:07:00,377
You said it wouldn't be a problem if
I joined only when I had the time.

86
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,117
You also said I could
quit whenever I wanted to.

87
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:06,377
Yes, I know what I said, but you've
been with us for a while now.

88
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,537
Everyone knows you.

89
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:11,502
If you leave us, it's going to
damage the reputation of the party.

90
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,200
Party members are not items.

91
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,760
What did you say?

92
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:30,397
Party members aren't items, so don't
expect them to be on call for you.

93
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,637
They're not your armor.

94
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,757
They're not your sword.

95
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,117
They're not your equipment.

96
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,480
You son of a...

97
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:40,037
I bet that big mouth of yours got
you thrown out of your own territory.

98
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,897
Let's see what you got, you
piece of spriggin' trash.

99
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:44,500
Okay, that's it. Enough.

100
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:48,200
Kirito's my new partner,
so leave him alone. What?

101
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:52,900
Leafa, you're abandoning us
to be a renegade like him?

102
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,300
Yes, I am.

103
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:58,186
And I'm not coming back ever.

104
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:02,977
I don't give a damn about you
buzzing around my party members.

105
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:06,397
But if you think you can steal
them, then that's another story.

106
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:09,297
If you're stupid enough to waltz
into another race's territory,

107
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:12,792
then it's your own damn fault
if you get killed, Spriggan!

108
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,876
This isn't the time or place, Sigurd.

109
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,176
If we gank this guy in front of all
these people, we're gonna look bad.

110
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:38,517
Once you cross our border, you
better run and hide, Leafa.

111
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:42,357
I never expected you to
betray me like this! Never.

112
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,720
But you'll regret it soon enough!

113
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:55,438
I'm really sorry you got
dragged into all that drama.

114
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,857
It's cool.

115
00:08:56,940 --> 00:08:58,677
I'm worried about you, though.

116
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,380
Are you sure about this?

117
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:05,540
Hey, don't!

118
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,470
Wow.

119
00:09:12,553 --> 00:09:14,100
This is an amazing view.

120
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:18,071
The sky's so close, it's like
I can reach out and touch it.

121
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:19,497
I know, right?

122
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:23,560
Whenever I look up at that sky,
everything else feels so small.

123
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:30,632
The timing couldn't have been any better.

124
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:33,377
I've been thinking about
leaving here for a while now.

125
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:38,284
Okay, but I feel like it's sort of my fault
you left on bad terms with those guys.

126
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:42,306
Yeah, well, I don't think it
could have happened any other way.

127
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,460
What do you mean by renegade?

128
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:49,120
A renegade's a player who
abandons their territory.

129
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:53,025
If you get branded as one,
everyone's going to look down on you.

130
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:54,829
And you're cool with that?

131
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:57,230
Yeah.

132
00:09:57,313 --> 00:09:58,143
I don't really care.

133
00:09:58,226 --> 00:10:02,057
But I don't understand why everyone's so
quick to tie each other down like that.

134
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:05,140
I mean, what's the point
in having wings, you know?

135
00:10:09,340 --> 00:10:11,297
You humans are so complicated.

136
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:13,597
Honestly, your psychology is confusing.

137
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:17,177
Why do you act so horribly to each other
when all you want is companionship?

138
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:18,257
What do you mean?

139
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:21,960
If it were me, I'd do that.

140
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,948
It's simple, straightforward,
and efficient.

141
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:27,060
And, uh, that's an amazing AI.

142
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:30,480
Do all private pixies act
like that, or just yours?

143
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,700
No, just mine, but she's a weirdo.

144
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,160
I guess you would know, huh?

145
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:39,040
All we want is companionship.

146
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:42,090
Lipia!

147
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:43,940
Hey, Recon.

148
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,500
How could you do this?

149
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:49,797
You could have at least said
something before you left.

150
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:51,527
Oh, sorry, I guess I forgot.

151
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,430
Aw.

152
00:10:53,513 --> 00:10:55,617
Why'd you quit the party
all of a sudden like that?

153
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:58,497
Well, I didn't really
think too hard about it.

154
00:10:58,580 --> 00:10:59,410
I just did it.

155
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,257
What are you going to do, though?

156
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:02,540
As if, Leafa!

157
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:04,317
It doesn't matter where you go.

158
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,357
My sword belongs to you and you alone.

159
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:08,280
I don't need it, but thanks.

160
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:10,690
Oh.

161
00:11:10,773 --> 00:11:13,157
What I meant by that was,
I'm going to go with you.

162
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,070
Wherever.

163
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:18,577
That is, I'd like to go, but there's
something that's been bugging me.

164
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:19,490
What is it?

165
00:11:19,573 --> 00:11:21,657
I can't really prove anything yet,

166
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:24,597
but there's a few things I
want to look into some more,

167
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,497
so I'm going to stay in
Sigurd's party a little longer.

168
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:28,620
Hey, Kirito?

169
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:31,517
She has a habit of getting
herself in trouble.

170
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,977
I'd appreciate it if
you'd keep an eye on her.

171
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:34,890
Yeah, sure.

172
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:36,240
Whatever you say.

173
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:40,551
And just to make sure we're
absolutely clear, Lipa is my...

174
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,577
We'll be in the neutral zone for a while.

175
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:47,542
Message me if you need anything.

176
00:11:57,980 --> 00:11:59,297
Let me get this straight.

177
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:00,757
In real life, he's your friend?

178
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,369
Yeah, something like that.

179
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:06,177
Okay, what's that weird
noise supposed to mean?

180
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:07,090
Nothing.

181
00:12:07,173 --> 00:12:08,840
Just a little jealous is all.

182
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:12,868
Now that person's
feelings I can understand.

183
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,433
He must like you a lot.

184
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:15,757
Wouldn't you say, Lipa?

185
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,899
Do you feel the same way about him?

186
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:21,260
Uh, I don't know, jeez!

187
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,040
Hurry up, you guys!

188
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:38,477
Let's try to make it all the way
to the lake without stopping!

189
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:39,390
Okay!

190
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:07,837
Unbelievable you can be so stubborn
seriously no matter what I do I can't

191
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:12,177
hurt you it's not like that body's
real why can't you just loosen up and

192
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:17,677
enjoy yourself a little I don't
expect you to understand but to me it

193
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:21,597
doesn't matter if my body's real or
virtual you may not think that way but

194
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:26,777
I do are you afraid you're going to
be corrupted somehow because if that's

195
00:13:26,860 --> 00:13:29,837
the case you definitely need to take
things a little less seriously while

196
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:33,477
you're here well I'm not planning on
staying in this cage forever you'll

197
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:39,840
see he'll come and save me really who
will that hero boyfriend of yours?

198
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:42,080
Goes by the name of Kirito.

199
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:45,750
Please.

200
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:47,397
You think I didn't know?

201
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:49,200
His real name's Kirigaya.

202
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,540
I met him the other
day, in the real world.

203
00:13:55,680 --> 00:14:00,497
I couldn't believe that weak little boy
was the same one who beat Sword Art Online.

204
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,815
It took me a second to collect myself.

205
00:14:02,900 --> 00:14:05,312
By the way, where do you think I met him?

206
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,437
In your hospital room.

207
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:11,402
As you were lying there, I told
him I'd be marrying you next week.

208
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,797
My God, you should have seen his face.

209
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,957
It was like all the
color drained out of it.

210
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:18,452
I could barely keep myself from laughing.

211
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,137
Do you want to know what I think?

212
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:24,257
I'll bet you anything that brat won't have

213
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:26,987
the guts to put on the
nerve gear ever again.

214
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,920
That reminds me.

215
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:33,297
I promised him I was going to
send along a wedding invitation.

216
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:34,917
I'm pretty sure he'll come.

217
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,437
He's going to want to see
you in your wedding dress.

218
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:39,100
I know. I'm generous.

219
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:42,633
The least I can do is leave
the little hero a few crumbs.

220
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:51,520
Well, I have to get going now, Titania.

221
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:53,940
I hope you don't miss me too much.

222
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:00,997
He's alive.

223
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,040
Kirito's alive.

224
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,350
Hm-hm.

225
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:36,300
8-1-1-3-2-3-2-9.

226
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:58,960
Nice job.

227
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,125
Thanks for the awesome backup.

228
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:06,657
Our wings aren't going
to last much longer.

229
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:08,797
I think we should land
down there for a bit.

230
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:09,710
Okay.

231
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:21,580
Hey, you getting tired
yet? Nope. I'm good to go.

232
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:23,180
Okay, Mr. Tough Guy.

233
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,417
I hate to break it to you, but flying's
out for both of us for a little while.

234
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:28,900
Huh? How come?

235
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:31,236
You see that mountain way over there?

236
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:34,017
It's above the altitude
limit, so we can't fly over.

237
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:37,477
The only way anyone can pass
it is to go through the caves.

238
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:41,077
It's the toughest part of the trip
between Sylph territory and Arun.

239
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,180
Or so I've heard.

240
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:44,716
I've never even been this far myself.

241
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:46,000
Guess we walk.

242
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:49,280
These caves, are they long? Pretty long.

243
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:51,677
There's a mining town about halfway.

244
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:54,097
It's neutral territory,
so we can rest there.

245
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,200
That reminds me.

246
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,357
Are you good for time, or
do you have to get back?

247
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,675
It's seven at night in the real world.

248
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,697
Yeah, I can keep going for a while.

249
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:02,610
Cool.

250
00:17:02,693 --> 00:17:04,244
I can too, so let's keep going.

251
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:06,797
But since we're here,
we should rotate out.

252
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,280
Wait, rotate? Yeah.

253
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:11,997
We take turns logging out and
resting while the other keeps watch.

254
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:14,577
You can't log out when you're
in the field, remember?

255
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:16,777
So we have to take turns logging out.

256
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:19,777
The person who stays behind
guards the other's avatar.

257
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:21,500
Okay, sounds like a plan.

258
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:22,970
Ladies first.

259
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:24,611
Okay, don't mind if I do.

260
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,727
See you in about 20 minutes.

261
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:53,505
Hey, Kazuto, what do you
want to do for dinner?

262
00:17:56,620 --> 00:17:58,300
I wonder if he's asleep.

263
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,840
I can't wait to get back there.

264
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,030
Kirito.

265
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,357
It's not that I'm in love
with him or anything,

266
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:43,381
or that I've got someone
to go on adventures with.

267
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,430
No.

268
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:47,880
I'm just excited I get to
go places in a new world.

269
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:01,420
Hey, I'm back!

270
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,151
Did you see any monsters?

271
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:04,460
No, I didn't.

272
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,777
It's been pretty quiet this whole time.

273
00:19:06,860 --> 00:19:07,997
What are you eating?

274
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:11,021
I bought a bunch at a shop
before we left Sylvain.

275
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:15,257
I don't know what they're called, but
an NPC said you can only get them there.

276
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:16,987
I've never seen them before.

277
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:31,337
Sorry to leave you like
this, but it is my turn.

278
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,580
Keep me safe, okay?

279
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,800
Get out of here before I hurt you!

280
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:52,120
No way!

281
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:54,177
You can move when your
master's logged out?

282
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:55,860
Well, of course I can move!

283
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,760
You know, I'm my own person!

284
00:19:58,040 --> 00:20:01,569
And for your information, he's
not my master, he's my daddy!

285
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,360
Yeah, about that.

286
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:06,677
I was gonna ask you before,
why do you call him your daddy?

287
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:09,860
Did he, you know, um, set
you that way or something?

288
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,497
He didn't do anything to my settings.

289
00:20:12,580 --> 00:20:13,480
He saved me.

290
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:15,565
He told me I was his daughter.

291
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:17,192
That makes him my daddy.

292
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:18,900
You see how that works?

293
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,520
Yeah, I guess.

294
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,540
Do you, you know, like him?

295
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,120
I'm sorry.

296
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:29,792
I don't understand what you mean by like.

297
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,520
Are you serious?

298
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:34,557
It means you want to be
with him all the time.

299
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:37,737
And when you're together, you
get excited about being near him.

300
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,580
Or something like that.

301
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:46,480
What's wrong, Leafa? Nothing!
It's nothing! What's nothing?

302
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:47,641
What's going on?

303
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:49,580
What is it?

304
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,375
Did something happen?

305
00:20:51,620 --> 00:20:52,840
Welcome back, Daddy.

306
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:56,797
Leafa was just explaining to me
what it means when someone said...

307
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:57,710
No!

308
00:20:57,793 --> 00:20:58,623
I said it's nothing!

309
00:20:58,706 --> 00:20:59,536
It's nothing!

310
00:20:59,619 --> 00:21:01,342
You weren't there for very long.

311
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,442
I hope you got something to eat.

312
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:04,370
Yeah.

313
00:21:04,453 --> 00:21:06,397
My family left something
for me, so I'm good.

314
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:08,900
Sweet. Come on, then. Let's get going.

315
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:14,920
Okay. All right. Lead the way.

316
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:19,420
Is something wrong? I don't know.

317
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,407
It sort of felt like
someone was watching us.

318
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:23,890
Hey, Yui.

319
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:25,611
There any players nearby?

320
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,955
No, I'm not sensing any other players.

321
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:31,160
Hmm, it's possible someone
put a tracer on us.

322
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:32,697
What the heck's a tracer?

323
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:34,251
A kind of tracking magic.

324
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:36,931
It looks like a small animal or an insect.

325
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,077
It tells the caster a target's position.

326
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,219
Can you dispel it?

327
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:42,000
Sure, if you can find it.

328
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:45,097
The thing is, if the
caster's magic skill is high,

329
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:47,177
the tracer can track you from far away.

330
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:50,260
In a field this size, it'd
take forever to find it.

331
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:51,330
Great.

332
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,824
Maybe it's just my imagination.

333
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,140
Come on, let's go. Okay.

334
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:09,757
Give me your hand I want

335
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:13,117
to lift those arms I want to

336
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:14,977
make my hands I want you to

337
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:21,540
I want you to I want you to

338
00:22:44,080 --> 00:22:46,880
Let's go.

339
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:01,597
I don't think you can hear what the end.

340
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:04,220
I'm not hearty,

341
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:08,840
I'm not hearty.

342
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:10,977
I'm not hearty, I'm hearty.

343
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:16,657
I'm hearty, I'm hearty.

344
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:23,380
I'm hearty.

345
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,800
Next time, the Lugru Corridor.
